From: Guard for PHP contributors
Subject: [PATCH] openssl: expose the existing legacy ASN1 const accessor in xp_ssl

Copyright (c) The PHP Group; PHP License 3.01.
Origin: PHP 8.2.35 ext/openssl/openssl.c, compatibility functions.
https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/php-8.2.35/ext/openssl/openssl.c

The signed PHP 8.2.35 source already uses this accessor in openssl.c.
Reuse the identical implementation and API-version guard in the separate
xp_ssl.c translation unit for OpenSSL 1.0.2. Peer-name and SAN validation
are unchanged. Newer OpenSSL and LibreSSL APIs keep their native accessor.

--- a/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
@@ -36,6 +36,14 @@
 #include <openssl/bn.h>
 #include <openssl/dh.h>
 
+#if PHP_OPENSSL_API_VERSION < 0x10100
+/* Same legacy const accessor as ext/openssl/openssl.c. */
+static const unsigned char *ASN1_STRING_get0_data(const ASN1_STRING *asn1)
+{
+	return M_ASN1_STRING_data(asn1);
+}
+#endif
+
 #ifdef PHP_WIN32
 #include "win32/winutil.h"
 #include "win32/time.h"
